tasks.summary:
I wrote the rules for the Sales and Catalog Reports area to /home/cloudcli/sourcecode/access-excel-to-django/northwind/analysis/rules/reports.json, with a reader version at /home/cloudcli/sourcecode/access-excel-to-django/northwind/analysis/rules/reports.md. All four acceptance commands pass.

- **Coverage:** every one of the 76 objects in scope has a decision: 35 keep and 41 drop. A check with rules-coverage against inventory.json found none of them uncovered.
- **Rules:** there are 16 rules, R-reports-001 to 016. Five are proven by equivalence (the four sales queries and the catalog query), eight by a rule test, and three by end-to-end tests.
- **Reports kept:** beside the invoice, which belongs to the orders area, I chose four reports: monthly sales per employee, monthly sales per product, quarterly sales per product, and the product catalog with its five sub-reports. These are recorded in two workflows, sales_reports and product_catalog.
- **Dropped:**
  - the employee email and phone lists, because the employee list page already shows those columns;
  - the Access learning page, its report, macro, menu entry and help-text table;
  - the table-diagram report and the report design template;
  - qrySales_SalesRep, which nothing uses;
  - the Access ribbon code and the report Activate/Close events, which only refresh the ribbon;
  - the catalog's scratch table of contents (Catalog_TableOfContents).
- **Other contents:** three services (sales_report_period, sales_report, product_catalog_pdf), one lookup (CompanyTypes.CompanyType, codes copied from the design, values null), three PROTECT relations, and seven open questions, Q-reports-001 to 007.
- **Possible bug in the original app:** order dates carry a time of day, but the sales reports compare them with an end date at midnight. Orders placed later on the end date are left out, and with the default period that includes the latest orders themselves. This is Q-reports-002.

